# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# Config secrets
config/oauth.json*
!config/oauth.json.example
.env

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Superpowers tool artifacts
.superpowers/
.worktrees/

# Simulation output (regenerable via simulate_draft.py)
data/sim_results/

# Season dashboard cache (populated at runtime)
data/cache/
data/cache_archive/

# Skill/luck data layer cache: MLB Stats API + Savant season pulls (re-fetchable)
data/skill_luck/

# Playing-time training panel: derived from the cached MLB pulls by
# scripts/build_pt_panel.py, and the live season moves it every rebuild.
data/playing_time/

# Trajectory comp panel: same generator, wider span, deliberately kept out of
# data/playing_time/ so it cannot become the keeper curve's training set. 8.3 MB of
# regenerable CSV that would otherwise re-diff on every rebuild.
# `/*` rather than `/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so a trailing-slash rule here makes the two negations below silently dead.
data/trajectory/*
# ...but the FITTED ARTIFACTS ship. They are 43 KB and 1 KB of JSON, not megabytes of
# CSV, and the deployed dashboard reads them off disk -- `load_shipped` /
# `load_shipped_bars` resolve `PROJECT_ROOT / data/trajectory/`. Without them Render
# has no band calibration and no realized bars, so the board silently falls back to the
# uncorrected band and prints no probabilities at all: the failure looks like a design
# choice rather than a missing file. They are also the only derived inputs a reviewer
# can diff, which is what makes a recalibration visible in a PR.
!data/trajectory/band_calibration.json
!data/trajectory/value_bars.json

# SQLite databases (populated at runtime), and their sidecars. The -wal/-shm
# pair is created whenever a WAL store is open, so `git add -A` during a run
# would otherwise stage SQLite internals -- including uncheckpointed pages of
# data/local.db, the Yahoo KV baseline. `data/*.db` does not cover them: the
# suffix comes AFTER the .db, so each needs its own pattern.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-journal

# Hot streak analysis: local DuckDB + research notebooks (not source of truth)
data/streaks/
notebooks/streaks/

# Generated manual-pipeline audit reports. The TRANSCRIPTIONS in data/manual/
# (standings.yaml, rosters.yaml, fa_exclusions.yaml) are deliberately tracked --
# they are hand-typed input worth reviewing in a diff. The dated report is a run
# artifact regenerated on every run, so it stays out.
# Every GENERATED report under data/manual/. The hand-typed transcriptions there
# (*.yaml) stay tracked -- they are input worth reviewing in a diff; the .txt
# reports are run artifacts regenerated on every run. Pattern is by extension so
# a new report type does not have to remember to add itself here.
data/manual/*.txt
